WEBVTT

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:10.469
Good news, everyone.
We've got a very special delivery today.

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:12.137
- Who's it going to?
- Me.

00:00:12.513 --> 00:00:14.681
Another job well done.

00:00:14.765 --> 00:00:19.144
No, I need it shipped to my office
at Mars University.

00:00:19.228 --> 00:00:22.648
It's a little experiment
that may well win me the Nobel Prize.

00:00:22.731 --> 00:00:23.732
In what field?

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:25.817
I don't care. They all pay the same.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:28.362
- Is it dangerous?
- Oh, my, no.

00:00:36.411 --> 00:00:37.788
Off we go.

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.834
Very impressive.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:27.880
Back in the 20th century, we had no idea
there was a university on Mars.

00:01:28.005 --> 00:01:30.883
Well, in those days,
Mars was just a dreary,

00:01:30.966 --> 00:01:34.261
uninhabitable wasteland, much like Utah.

00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:37.431
But unlike Utah,
it was eventually made livable

00:01:37.514 --> 00:01:40.976
when the university was founded in 2636.

00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:43.437
They planted traditional college foliage,

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.731
ivy, trees, hemp.

00:01:45.814 --> 00:01:47.482
Soon, the whole planet was terra-formed.

00:01:47.566 --> 00:01:49.610
Does that mean
it's safe to breathe the air?

00:01:49.693 --> 00:01:50.736
Of course.

00:01:54.865 --> 00:01:57.576
Over here is Wong Library.

00:01:57.701 --> 00:02:01.955
It has the largest collection
of literature in the western universe.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.504
Hey, look. There's a chapter
of my old robot fraternity.

00:02:08.587 --> 00:02:10.506
Epsilon rho rho.

00:02:10.589 --> 00:02:11.965
You went to college?

00:02:12.049 --> 00:02:15.052
Of course. I'm a bender.
I went to bending college.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.595
I majored in bending.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.473
- What was your minor?
- Robo-American studies.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.186
Are you here to fumigate the moose head?

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:28.023
Uh, no. Actually,
I'm an epsilon from way back.

00:02:35.113 --> 00:02:37.157
Eh. Close enough. Come on in.

00:02:37.241 --> 00:02:39.618
Thanks. Here's your finger back.

00:02:40.661 --> 00:02:43.872
All the coolest robots
are in this fraternity.

00:02:44.581 --> 00:02:47.626
Mate in 143 moves.

00:02:47.751 --> 00:02:50.212
Poo. You win again.

00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:52.339
Oh! Nerds.

00:02:52.422 --> 00:02:54.049
Allow me to introduce myself.

00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:56.301
I'm Gearshift, chapter president.

00:02:56.385 --> 00:02:58.428
This is Oily, and this here is Fat-Bot.

00:02:58.512 --> 00:03:00.889
You're all losers. My name's Bender.

00:03:02.057 --> 00:03:04.351
Bender from Bending State Bender?

00:03:04.476 --> 00:03:06.645
Wow! You're a legend around here.

00:03:06.728 --> 00:03:08.397
I heard that in one single night,

00:03:08.522 --> 00:03:10.941
you drank a whole keg,
streaked across campus

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.652
and crammed 58 humans into a phone booth.

00:03:13.735 --> 00:03:17.364
Yeah, well, a lot of them were children.

00:03:17.447 --> 00:03:18.991
Anyway, I should get going.

00:03:19.074 --> 00:03:21.869
No, Bender, wait.
We're the lamest frat on campus.

00:03:21.952 --> 00:03:24.413
Even Hillel has better parties than us.

00:03:24.496 --> 00:03:27.040
Please, you've got to stay
and teach us how to be cool.

00:03:27.249 --> 00:03:28.250
Mmm.

00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:31.461
Okay, but I'll need 10 kegs of beer,

00:03:31.545 --> 00:03:33.380
a continuous tape of Louie Louie

00:03:33.505 --> 00:03:36.550
and a regulation
two-story, panty-raid ladder.

00:03:36.633 --> 00:03:38.802
Oh, boy, oh, boy, oh, boy.

00:03:39.469 --> 00:03:42.431
I tell you, being here
really takes me back

00:03:42.514 --> 00:03:44.099
to my college days.

00:03:49.563 --> 00:03:52.733
Step right up. Who wants to learn physics?

00:03:56.904 --> 00:03:59.865
Keep your hands
inside the car at all times.

00:03:59.948 --> 00:04:03.493
Good old Coney Island College.
Go, whitefish!

00:04:03.577 --> 00:04:05.787
Don't take this the wrong way, Fry,
but you don't seem

00:04:05.871 --> 00:04:10.834
- like the educated type.
- Oh, yeah? Read it and weep.

00:04:11.668 --> 00:04:13.754
I'm a certified college dropout.

00:04:13.879 --> 00:04:16.757
Please. Everyone knows
20th century colleges

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:19.051
were basically expensive day care centers.

00:04:19.134 --> 00:04:22.054
That's true.
By current academic standards,

00:04:22.137 --> 00:04:24.306
you're merely a high school dropout.

00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:26.683
What? That's not fair.

00:04:26.767 --> 00:04:30.187
I deserve the same respect
any other college dropout gets.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.315
By God, I'm going to enroll here
at Mars University

00:04:33.398 --> 00:04:35.150
and drop out all over again.

00:04:35.234 --> 00:04:36.944
You won't last two weeks.

00:04:37.069 --> 00:04:39.446
Ah! Thanks for believing in me.

00:04:45.994 --> 00:04:47.955
Yo, classmate, whatcha taking?

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:49.540
Oh, I don't know.

00:04:49.665 --> 00:04:51.708
Professor, what are you
teaching this semester?

00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:53.877
Same thing I teach every semester.

00:04:53.961 --> 00:04:56.797
The mathematics
of quantum neutrino fields.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.925
I made up the title
so that no student would dare take it.

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:04.638
"Mathematics of wonton burrito meals."
I'll be there.

00:05:04.721 --> 00:05:06.765
Please, Fry. I don't know how to teach.

00:05:06.849 --> 00:05:08.350
I'm a professor.

00:05:08.433 --> 00:05:09.685
See you in class.

00:05:26.869 --> 00:05:28.620
This is gonna be great.

00:05:37.921 --> 00:05:40.215
- Bingo.
- Oh, Mama.

00:05:43.093 --> 00:05:46.054
Oh, yeah. Someone's been a bad computer.

00:05:48.015 --> 00:05:49.224
Get a load of that.

00:05:56.064 --> 00:05:59.318
I say, you've damaged
our servants quarters

00:05:59.401 --> 00:06:00.944
and our servants.

00:06:01.028 --> 00:06:05.032
This time, Robot House has gone too far.

00:06:05.115 --> 00:06:06.116
Cheese it!

00:06:11.705 --> 00:06:14.041
Hey, pretty nice for a single.

00:06:14.124 --> 00:06:16.668
Two desks, two chairs, a couple of beds...

00:06:16.752 --> 00:06:18.545
A woodpecker.

00:06:18.629 --> 00:06:20.589
I think that's probably your roommate.

00:06:20.964 --> 00:06:23.759
Right, cool. Come on in, roomie.

00:06:25.135 --> 00:06:26.428
Huh?

00:06:26.553 --> 00:06:28.972
- What the...
- I call top bunk.

00:06:29.681 --> 00:06:31.600
Ah!

00:06:37.356 --> 00:06:40.651
- My roommate's a monkey?
- Brilliant deduction.

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:43.070
You're a credit to your species.

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:45.739
Ah, Fry. I see you've met Guenter.

00:06:45.864 --> 00:06:47.366
You know each other?

00:06:47.491 --> 00:06:49.284
Guenter is my experiment.

00:06:49.368 --> 00:06:52.829
He was the top-secret contents
of this stinking crate.

00:06:52.913 --> 00:06:56.458
I'd rather live in a crate
than share a room with this dork.

00:06:57.251 --> 00:07:00.629
- So, what makes Guenter talk?
- Is he genetically engineered?

00:07:00.754 --> 00:07:05.342
Oh, please. That's preposterous
science fiction mumbo jumbo.

00:07:05.425 --> 00:07:08.929
Guenter's intelligence actually lies
in his electronium hat

00:07:09.012 --> 00:07:13.392
which harnesses the power of sunspots
to produce cognitive radiation.

00:07:14.768 --> 00:07:19.022
You're wasting your breath, Professor.
he'll never understand a word of it.

00:07:19.106 --> 00:07:20.691
I understood the word "hat."

00:07:21.066 --> 00:07:22.734
Please, stop bickering.

00:07:22.818 --> 00:07:25.320
I arranged that you be roommates
for a reason...

00:07:25.404 --> 00:07:27.865
So I'd only have to remember
one phone number.

00:07:27.948 --> 00:07:29.950
Now shake hands and make up.

00:07:31.702 --> 00:07:33.203
You want a banana?

00:07:33.287 --> 00:07:34.705
I don't eat bananas.

00:07:34.788 --> 00:07:38.125
I prefer banana-flavored
energy bars made from tofu.

00:07:38.876 --> 00:07:40.252
I don't like you.

00:07:47.718 --> 00:07:50.429
This is gonna be a cake walk.

00:07:50.554 --> 00:07:53.390
Welcome to the history
of the 20th century.

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:55.809
Look to your left, then to your right.

00:07:55.893 --> 00:07:58.145
Then in nine other directions.

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:01.565
One of the 12 of you
will not pass this class.

00:08:01.648 --> 00:08:05.194
Boring. Let's hear about
Walter Mondale already.

00:08:05.277 --> 00:08:09.281
Be forewarned. The only sure way
to get an A in this class

00:08:09.406 --> 00:08:11.783
is to have lived in the 20th century.

00:08:11.867 --> 00:08:12.868
Swish.

00:08:16.538 --> 00:08:18.457
You were saying, Mr. Fry?

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:21.877
I'm from the 20th century.
Go ahead. Ask me anything.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:25.464
Very well. What device invented
in the 20th century

00:08:25.589 --> 00:08:29.635
allowed people to view broadcast programs
in their own homes?

00:08:29.968 --> 00:08:33.972
Oh! I know this.
What do you call it? Lite-Brite.

00:08:36.642 --> 00:08:39.228
I believe the answer is the television.

00:08:39.311 --> 00:08:42.523
Very good, Mr. Guenter.

00:08:42.648 --> 00:08:45.400
Wow. Smart and cute.

00:08:51.365 --> 00:08:54.159
What I love about being dean of students

00:08:54.243 --> 00:08:57.079
is the peace and quiet
and the respect I receive.

00:08:58.288 --> 00:08:59.790
Now, what's all this about?

00:08:59.915 --> 00:09:03.168
Dean Vernon, the students
from Robot House are here.

00:09:03.252 --> 00:09:05.045
Robot House.

00:09:05.128 --> 00:09:07.714
Hey, Dean. Nice looking model.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.132
You keep away from it.

00:09:09.216 --> 00:09:12.094
You robots are a disgrace
to this university.

00:09:12.219 --> 00:09:16.014
Whenever a fire alarm is pulled,
it's Robot House.

00:09:16.098 --> 00:09:19.518
Whenever the campus liquor store
is looted, Robot House.

00:09:19.601 --> 00:09:21.937
Whenever a human corpse is desecrated...

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.730
Now, I can explain that.

00:09:23.814 --> 00:09:25.065
That's enough out of you.

00:09:25.148 --> 00:09:26.483
From this day forth,

00:09:26.567 --> 00:09:30.487
Robot House is on dodeca-tuple
secret probation.

00:09:30.612 --> 00:09:33.073
- No fair.
- My mom is gonna kill me.

00:09:33.156 --> 00:09:34.700
Now, if you'll excuse me,

00:09:34.825 --> 00:09:37.369
I have to get back to the one
thing that's kept me sane

00:09:37.452 --> 00:09:40.330
these past eight years, my model ship.

00:09:41.832 --> 00:09:43.667
Fat-Bot, no!

00:09:44.835 --> 00:09:47.171
When I get nervous, I get hungry.

00:09:48.130 --> 00:09:49.214
Cheese it!

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:52.801
Robot House!

00:09:54.636 --> 00:09:57.598
So, Chrissy,
we seem to be hitting it off.

00:09:57.681 --> 00:10:00.726
If you're not doing anything later,
might I escort you to a kegger?

00:10:00.809 --> 00:10:03.312
Not even if you were the last man on Mars.

00:10:13.614 --> 00:10:15.908
Hey, you like bananas?

00:10:16.575 --> 00:10:19.661
I got her number.
How do you like them bananas?

00:10:22.289 --> 00:10:25.584
And therefore, by process of elimination,

00:10:25.667 --> 00:10:28.462
the electron must taste like grape-ade.

00:10:29.296 --> 00:10:31.423
Sorry. I overslept.

00:10:31.507 --> 00:10:33.383
Until 5:00 p.m.?

00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:35.010
It's that obnoxious monkey.

00:10:35.093 --> 00:10:37.846
He kept me up all night
with his constant thinking.

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.890
Just thinking and thinking.

00:10:39.973 --> 00:10:41.808
He's trying to make me look like an idiot.

00:10:41.892 --> 00:10:44.603
Don't be jealous. Without his special hat,

00:10:44.686 --> 00:10:47.314
Guenter might be no more
intelligent than you.

00:10:47.564 --> 00:10:49.900
I hate that rodent.

00:10:50.025 --> 00:10:53.529
Fry, that monkey
is my most important experiment.

00:10:53.654 --> 00:10:56.949
If you two don't stop fighting,
I'll have you both neutered.

00:10:57.324 --> 00:10:59.159
That'll show him.

00:11:06.291 --> 00:11:09.753
Dean Vernon, I'd like you
to meet my parents, Leo and Inez.

00:11:09.878 --> 00:11:13.048
Ah! Mr. and Mrs. Wong.
I'm so glad we could admit Amy

00:11:13.131 --> 00:11:15.843
in exchange
for your generous contribution.

00:11:15.926 --> 00:11:18.136
How much more for phi beta kappa?

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:19.638
How much you got?

00:11:22.057 --> 00:11:25.269
Sorry I'm late.
I was off at a study session

00:11:25.352 --> 00:11:26.895
with Chrissy.

00:11:29.857 --> 00:11:31.775
Oh, I'm glad you made it, Guenter,

00:11:31.859 --> 00:11:33.861
because in honor of parents weekend,

00:11:33.944 --> 00:11:36.613
I have a special surprise for you.

00:11:37.406 --> 00:11:40.200
Mom! Dad! What are you doing here?

00:11:43.954 --> 00:11:46.123
This is so humiliating.

00:11:46.999 --> 00:11:49.084
Now, these monkeys I like.

00:11:51.545 --> 00:11:53.755
What's that? You want to come out?

00:11:55.424 --> 00:11:56.717
No! Stop!

00:12:02.973 --> 00:12:04.224
I say.

00:12:04.308 --> 00:12:06.518
What's that they're flinging at us?

00:12:06.643 --> 00:12:09.396
Dear lord. All over the dean.

00:12:09.479 --> 00:12:12.316
Hey, why don't you get up
on the chandelier with your parents

00:12:12.399 --> 00:12:13.567
and I'll take a picture.

00:12:15.235 --> 00:12:16.445
Oh!

00:12:17.946 --> 00:12:20.157
Well, looks like
this party's winding down.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:23.827
Let's take a road trip to Tijuana
and get Fat-Bot some action.

00:12:26.038 --> 00:12:28.498
It's my first time. I'm really nervous.

00:12:32.461 --> 00:12:34.630
Robot House!

00:12:37.382 --> 00:12:39.676
What you did to Guenter was cruel.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:42.221
At the risk of sounding
like an after-school special,

00:12:42.346 --> 00:12:45.098
I think we learned
who the real animal was today.

00:12:45.182 --> 00:12:46.767
You mean peer pressure?

00:12:47.935 --> 00:12:50.145
Look out. He's got a gun!

00:12:52.064 --> 00:12:53.524
Leave me alone.

00:12:53.607 --> 00:12:57.069
Hey, what's going on?
I thought you didn't like bananas.

00:12:57.152 --> 00:12:58.862
Of course I do.

00:12:58.987 --> 00:13:03.575
I try so hard to fit in,
but seeing my parents act like that

00:13:03.659 --> 00:13:07.204
made me realize
I'm just a primitive beast.

00:13:07.287 --> 00:13:10.624
Hey, hey, cheer up.
Not everyone turns out like their parents.

00:13:10.791 --> 00:13:14.169
I mean, look at me.
My folks were honest, hardworking people.

00:13:14.711 --> 00:13:17.548
Besides, Guenter,
you're not like other monkeys.

00:13:17.631 --> 00:13:18.966
You've got the hat.

00:13:19.091 --> 00:13:23.387
So what? I mean, sure,
it looks cool and it makes me smart,

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:25.973
but it doesn't make me happy.

00:13:27.975 --> 00:13:29.852
That's so sad.

00:13:30.018 --> 00:13:32.104
I didn't even know monkeys could cry.

00:13:32.187 --> 00:13:34.773
They can't. It's all the hat.

00:13:38.819 --> 00:13:41.363
Look, Guenter,
if you're so miserable here,

00:13:41.446 --> 00:13:43.574
maybe you should just
go back to the jungle.

00:13:44.324 --> 00:13:45.617
The jungle...

00:13:46.743 --> 00:13:50.455
But I couldn't do that to the professor.
I'm his prized experiment.

00:13:50.539 --> 00:13:52.332
And he's like a father to me.

00:13:52.416 --> 00:13:54.042
But he's not your father.

00:13:54.126 --> 00:13:56.378
That guy in the punch bowl
was your father.

00:14:03.886 --> 00:14:06.555
Look at him. I'm so proud.

00:14:06.638 --> 00:14:07.806
Thanks, Professor.

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:09.099
Not you.

00:14:09.183 --> 00:14:10.392
Ow!

00:14:51.141 --> 00:14:54.269
Oh! I always feared he might
run off like this.

00:14:54.937 --> 00:14:57.231
Why? Why?

00:14:57.314 --> 00:15:00.192
Why didn't I break his legs?

00:15:07.574 --> 00:15:09.743
Oh, poor Guenter.

00:15:09.826 --> 00:15:12.871
So, he just ran away
in the middle of the exam?

00:15:12.955 --> 00:15:14.456
I'm afraid so.

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:18.126
All he handed in was a paper
smeared with feces.

00:15:18.293 --> 00:15:19.878
He tied with Fry.

00:15:19.962 --> 00:15:21.338
I guess he realized I was right

00:15:21.421 --> 00:15:23.173
when I told him to go back to the jungle.

00:15:23.257 --> 00:15:25.884
You what? After I spent months

00:15:26.009 --> 00:15:28.387
slaving over a hot monkey brain?

00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:29.763
Hey, don't blame me.

00:15:29.888 --> 00:15:33.016
You tried to force Guenter to be a human,
but he's an animal.

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:36.895
He belongs in the wild. Or in the circus
on one of those tiny tricycles.

00:15:36.979 --> 00:15:39.064
Now that's entertainment.

00:15:39.147 --> 00:15:42.442
But Guenter's obviously
better off being intelligent.

00:15:42.568 --> 00:15:44.027
Tell him, Leela.

00:15:44.486 --> 00:15:47.155
Uh-uh. I'm staying out of this.
Now, here's my opinion.

00:15:47.239 --> 00:15:48.740
What we should do is...

00:15:51.201 --> 00:15:52.202
What?

00:15:52.286 --> 00:15:56.290
I said we'll go to the jungle
and let Guenter decide once and for all.

00:15:56.415 --> 00:15:57.708
What?

00:16:04.214 --> 00:16:05.465
You all know the rules.

00:16:05.549 --> 00:16:09.011
Whichever house wins the regatta
becomes head of the Greek council.

00:16:09.094 --> 00:16:12.014
And should that house
currently be on any type of

00:16:12.139 --> 00:16:16.018
multiple secret probation,
it will be lifted

00:16:16.101 --> 00:16:18.937
and I will be forced
to serve as grand marshal

00:16:19.021 --> 00:16:21.356
of a parade honoring them.

00:16:22.107 --> 00:16:24.234
I say, Robot House,

00:16:24.318 --> 00:16:28.322
your watercraft is as ill-designed
as you yourselves.

00:16:28.405 --> 00:16:29.698
Good one, Chet.

00:16:34.995 --> 00:16:37.206
Oh, yeah? Watch this.

00:16:44.296 --> 00:16:46.173
Well, I never.

00:16:46.298 --> 00:16:49.426
Fraternities, on your marks.

00:16:51.678 --> 00:16:52.846
Hey.

00:16:56.558 --> 00:16:59.978
Wow, the jungles on Mars
look just like the jungles on Earth.

00:17:00.062 --> 00:17:01.605
Jungles on Earth?

00:17:04.107 --> 00:17:06.652
I see some movement up there.
I think it's him.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:08.320
Stand back.

00:17:15.661 --> 00:17:16.662
Oops.

00:17:16.745 --> 00:17:20.707
Don't worry, they'll be fine
once the tranquilizer wears off.

00:17:25.295 --> 00:17:26.755
There's our man.

00:17:29.383 --> 00:17:33.428
Professor, you'll offer Guenter the hat,
and, Fry, you'll offer him the banana.

00:17:33.512 --> 00:17:35.931
We'll let him choose
whether he wants to be intelligent

00:17:36.056 --> 00:17:37.391
or just a mindless animal.

00:17:37.558 --> 00:17:38.809
Mmm, mmm.

00:17:42.396 --> 00:17:44.398
Come on, Guenter, take the hat.

00:17:44.481 --> 00:17:46.149
No, the banana, the banana.

00:17:46.233 --> 00:17:49.611
Consider the philosophical
and metaphysical ramifications of the...

00:17:49.695 --> 00:17:51.071
Banana, banana, banana.

00:17:51.154 --> 00:17:52.698
Wait. What's that sound?

00:17:56.535 --> 00:17:58.954
Hey, Bender,
are you sure this is a shortcut?

00:17:59.037 --> 00:18:01.206
Not as sure as I was an hour ago.

00:18:20.017 --> 00:18:21.643
And the winner is...

00:18:23.687 --> 00:18:25.814
Robot House?

00:18:26.398 --> 00:18:28.233
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

00:18:36.909 --> 00:18:39.369
- Oh, no!
- Help!

00:18:42.623 --> 00:18:45.167
Thank God this log is sturdy.

00:18:47.169 --> 00:18:48.170
Oh!

00:18:53.467 --> 00:18:56.929
Put on the hat, Guenter!
You're the only one who can save us!

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:03.018
Stupid monkey.

00:19:05.687 --> 00:19:07.356
- No!
- Not there.

00:19:07.481 --> 00:19:08.982
Keep trying.

00:19:14.238 --> 00:19:17.366
Eureka! The hat goes on the head.

00:19:17.491 --> 00:19:19.493
It's all so obvious now.

00:19:20.494 --> 00:19:21.954
Help us, Guenter!

00:19:22.037 --> 00:19:23.288
Oh, my goodness.

00:19:23.413 --> 00:19:26.083
Hang on! I need to do some calculations!

00:19:26.166 --> 00:19:28.085
The decimal goes...

00:19:28.168 --> 00:19:30.003
Carry the seven... Got it!

00:19:40.347 --> 00:19:41.515
Grab on!

00:19:44.184 --> 00:19:47.479
- We're saved.
- Appreciate it, Guenter.

00:19:50.107 --> 00:19:53.735
Oh, no! Hurry, Guenter. Climb up the vine!

00:19:53.819 --> 00:19:55.445
You can still save yourself!

00:19:55.529 --> 00:19:58.699
Why bother? I've got nothing to live for.

00:19:58.949 --> 00:20:01.535
I was miserable as a genius.

00:20:01.618 --> 00:20:05.289
And as a monkey, I was so dumb
I tried to wear a hat on my butt.

00:20:07.124 --> 00:20:10.335
There's just no place
for me in this world.

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:12.671
Although, on the other hand...

00:20:19.678 --> 00:20:22.389
Oh, that poor, sweet monkey.

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:26.518
Well, let's go gather him up.
There's no sense letting him go to waste.

00:20:29.271 --> 00:20:31.356
Guenter, you're alive.

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:34.067
I guess the hat must have broke my fall.

00:20:35.235 --> 00:20:39.072
It seems to be working
at only half capacity, but I can fix it.

00:20:39.198 --> 00:20:41.825
No, wait! I like it like this.

00:20:41.909 --> 00:20:44.286
I actually feel sort of happy.

00:20:44.369 --> 00:20:47.247
But what about your super intelligence?

00:20:47.372 --> 00:20:50.209
When I had that,
there was too much pressure to use it.

00:20:50.292 --> 00:20:51.919
All I want out of life is to be

00:20:52.044 --> 00:20:54.671
a monkey of moderate intelligence
who wears a suit.

00:20:54.755 --> 00:20:57.674
That's why I've decided to
transfer to business school.

00:20:57.758 --> 00:21:01.803
No!

00:21:09.937 --> 00:21:12.064
Come on, everyone!

00:21:12.147 --> 00:21:15.192
Big party at Robot House!

00:21:15.275 --> 00:21:17.110
- You know you make me wanna
-Shout

00:21:17.194 --> 00:21:18.779
-Kick my heels up and
-Shout

00:21:18.904 --> 00:21:20.906
-Throw my hands up and
-Shout

00:21:21.031 --> 00:21:22.658
-Throw my head back and
-Shout

00:21:22.741 --> 00:21:23.951
Come on, now

00:21:24.034 --> 00:21:25.661
Don't forget to say you will

00:21:28.956 --> 00:21:31.250
Yeah, yeah, yeah

00:21:34.628 --> 00:21:35.921
Say you will

00:21:39.132 --> 00:21:40.843
Say that you

00:21:44.221 --> 00:21:46.431
Say that you need me